  "$comment": "P4.D217 — the Scenario Builder REST edge's route family. v4's REAL route (real middleware, real repositories over a per-case copy of the committed chat-send fixture pair with these plants applied) with ONLY runScenarioBuilder canned to `frames` (the one place a mock is right: the route's contract is what it does AROUND the run) and, for one case, resolveScenarioBuilderCapabilities throwing. v5: the real axum edge over the same planted instance, with a canned DRIVER publishing the same frames. The first 18 names are v4's route.test.ts cases (split where one v4 case asks two things); the last five are the middleware's. P4.D231 (v4 08c49319d): the chat-send pair carries NO `groups` table, so the plants create it (v4's own DDL, IF NOT EXISTS) with a readable group (Aeronauts Club) and an unreadable, BLOB-named one; the fourth id is never planted. P4.139: a fifth profile clone whose name is a BLOB (X'00') — v4's `findById` (a fallback-mode `safeQuery` over `_findById`) refuses the Float32-decoded name and logs `Error finding entity by ID {collection: 'connection_profiles', id, error}`; v5's `marshal_cp_row` refuses the BLOB and `scenario_builder_prepare` logs the same line through `db::fallback::find_by_id_or_none`. Both then answer the 404 with the route's DEBUG.",
